From 0a72c04ee7f4e3986e6c3d77e1874d29ebb56342 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:11:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] datamap: fix what the independent review found

DataMapStore.restore failed with a NullPointerException on the service thread when it restored no rows
into a user that had nothing yet. A cleared history leaves an empty day in the file, so the next unlock
of that user took down the system server.

The store kept the full host name of every lookup instead of its service key, so a name with a random
label made a new entry and evicted the real ones of that app. DNS contacts are now stored under their
service key.

netd reports an IPv4 connect of a Java socket as ::ffff:a.b.c.d while the DNS answer is a.b.c.d, so
every connect was counted again. Both forms are one address now. The recent answers are kept per app, so
that one app cannot push out the answers of another, and are forgotten when a user is cleared or stopped.

The reply to the app was not bounded and could exceed the Binder transaction limit: it carries at most
2000 entries and 300 links. The earlier days of the history are read once per change of the file, not at
every call, and the cache is dropped when the app unregisters.

The last minute of the history is written when the user is stopping (the storage is locked right after
onUserStopped) and when the device shuts down. The settings of a user change atomically.
